// NCAA lacrosse programs — men's and women's, Divisions I / II / III.
//
// Second sport dataset for the shared map engine (see js/sports.js). Same record
// shape as js/data.js so every renderer, filter, and tool works unchanged. The
// key differences from hockey: lacrosse has THREE NCAA divisions (D1/D2/D3), and
// there is no club-league tier here yet (MCLA/WCLA are deferred).
//
// Exported as `LACROSSE_SCHOOLS` — a DISTINCT name from data.js's `SCHOOLS`,
// because tools/build-standalone.cjs flattens every module into one shared scope
// and a second `export const SCHOOLS` would collide (see the esc-scoping note in
// js/leafmap.js).
//
// `id` is the campus key and is deliberately SHARED with js/data.js where a
// school fields both sports (e.g. "cornell", "williams", "rit") — that shared id
// is what powers the "also plays hockey here" cross-sport link. Schools that only
// play lacrosse (Penn, Maryland, Salisbury, …) get fresh ids + coordinates.
//
// PHASE 1a — this is a small hand-verified SAMPLE (Ivy men + Ivy/Big Ten women,
// plus a few D2/D3) to prove the schema/UI end-to-end. The full ~900-program
// dataset is gathered in a follow-up pass (see the plan). `hockeyUrl` is the
// generic athletics-program link the detail card renders; null falls back to a
// search link rather than shipping a guessed URL.

